    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm trying to set up some reorder logic for our lithium-ion battery components. We get a lot of lead time variability from our suppliers in Shenzhen, so I need to figure out a solid way to calculate safety stock levels so we don't hit stockouts during our peak seasonal demand. Can you help me with a formula or a framework for this?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A robust approach is to calculate safety stock based on the variability of both demand and lead time, rather than using a fixed buffer. A common formula involves multiplying the desired service level's Z-score by the square root of (Average Lead Time $\\times$ Demand Variance + Average Demand $\\times$ Lead Time Variance). This allows you to scientifically account for upstream disruptions and fluctuating customer needs. Regularly reviewing your supplier performance data is crucial to keep the variance inputs accurate.",
