      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For those truly \"unknown unknowns,\" you need to model resilience rather than just variability, which points towards incorporating risk tolerance directly. You can implement a higher-tier buffer, often called a \"strategic contingency stock,\" based on expert judgment or historical disaster frequency, separate from the statistical safety stock. This contingency acts as an insurance policy against systemic issues outside your immediate data capture. Periodically review your supply chain mapping to identify potential single points of failure that could create those unseen delays.",
      "source": "target",
